## Lore

Folk of the Deep South often take the Septumbrans, the Witch Wolves, for
demons or were-beasts out of the Rifts, but they are flesh and blood
D-Bees. They are huge, seven to nine feet of muscle with slavering jaws,
jet black to dark grey fur, pale faces and bellies, a shaggy mane and a
long, furred, serpent-like tail as long as they are tall.

Their dreadful reputation is mostly earned. Most Witch Wolves revel in
robbery, murder and cruelty, keep pens of human and D-Bee captives to
eat, and take up work as bandits, assassins and dark sorcerers; at least
half practise black magic such as witchery, shifting and necromancy,
which is where their nickname comes from. They are as clever as humans,
which makes them worse.

Unlike most D-Bees they have kept their culture whole, and it is built on
enslavement, death, demon worship and veneration of the dead. Families
keep their ancestors'' ashes in a communal urn, and anyone leaving home
carries a pouch of those ashes for luck. They dress in sleeveless robes,
trench coats and ragged kilts, love Vibro-Blades, lasers and plasma
weapons, and live in their own remote communities from eastern Texas to
the Florida Panhandle. Fewer than a thousand are believed to exist.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character or NPC.

Favoured O.C.C.s: half are practitioners of magic or a related O.C.C.:
Necromancer (20%), Shifter (25%), Witch (25%), Mystic (5%), Mystic Knight
(5%), Ley Line Walker (5%), Blood Priest (3%), Elemental Fusionist (2%),
Conjurer (2%) or other (8%); few become Warlocks or Techno-Wizards.
Others: Bandit, Highway Man, Bounty Hunter, Headhunter (not Momano),
Mercenary Soldier, Pecos Raider, Pirate, Pirate Slaver, River Pirate,
Dragon Juicer and Maxi-Juicer (super rare), Professional Gambler,
Trapper-Woodsman, Vagabond and Wilderness Scout. Psionic O.C.C.s are
uncommon but exist.

Size 7-9 feet (2.1 to 2.7 m). Weight 370-650 pounds (167 to 293 kg). Life
span 3D6+62 years for males, 3D6+70 for females; mature by 11. NPC
experience level 1D6+1. Pronounced SEPT-umm-brans; also called Witch
Wolves, Black Magic Wolves and Necro-Wolves.

Habitat: the southern Old American Empire, thickest in the northern
forests of Alabama and Mississippi, especially the Hamlet of Clavicle;
thought to have come through a Rift at the ley line nexus near old Selma.
Slave market value 5D6x10,000, +40% for a mage and +60% for a psychic.

Allies: they keep to their own kind but will deal with evil and magical
beings of every sort - Brodkil, Black Faeries, Witchlings, Lesser Demons -
trade slaves with Horune Pirates and Splugorth Slavers, and may serve a
Neuron Beast, Demon Lord, dark god or Alien Intelligence if given rank.
Enemies: Cyber-Knights and heroes of renown; they look down on humans and
other D-Bees, and treat the Federation of Magic as a rival.
